==Strategy==
The enemies in this stage are incredibly dangerous, with Shadow relentlessly laying down fire from afar (500 range with 550 Omni Strike) while they constantly assault the frontline. Given Shadow's very high speed and Slow Immunity, any ground he gains would be difficult to recover (in spite of his 5 knockbacks), and the likes of Cyberpunk are not available. Complicating matters is the appearance of Zang Roo and Zir Zeal, both of whom could burrow far beyond the player's units, potentially reaching and destroying the Cat Base before Shadow even gets there. Thankfully, the peons in the stage will eventually dry up, at which point Shadow can be easily stalled as various units chip away at him.

As with the preceding stages, most of the threats spawn on base hit, so it's theoretically possible to also pin Shadow at the base with [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bomber]] then quickly whittle him down and destroy the base before the other enemies arrive. This can be done with assistance from the Thunderbolt Cannon, all Void Fruit Treasures maxed and a Freeze Up M Combo, ensuring only one Bomber is needed to Perma-Freeze Shadow, provided if the support are dealt with, or if enough DPS can be accumulated to kill off Shadow before the other threats reach Bomber.
